 measurement: exchange_flux_and_growth_rate (bands to be sharpened before run).", "measure": "exchange_flux_and_growth_rate"}, {"name": "study-selection-for-proximity-fitness-gain-relative-to-no-exchange", "classification": "secondary", "description": "Preregistered measurement: fitness_gain_relative_to_no_exchange (bands to be sharpened before run).", "measure": "fitness_gain_relative_to_no_exchange"}], "visualizations": [], "findings": [{"id": "s-sel-exchange-selects-contact", "statement": "Under metabolic exchange, a heritable contact/adhesion propensity is POSITIVELY selected (selection coefficient +0.63, contact fixes) above a frequency-dependent invasion threshold; the matched no-exchange control shows NEGATIVE selection (-0.36, contact eliminated). Exchange is necessary for selection-for-contact. Supports H1-syntrophy-first in the favorable regime; rejects H4-no-integration there.", "status": "confirms", "evidence": {"observed": 0.6264, "from_test": "study-selection-for-proximity-discriminates", "from_run": "proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid coupled-selection (exchange on) vs coupled-no-exchange control, seed 1"}, "inferential_scope": "Reduced coupled model (replicator on contact propensity; frequency-dependent exchange benefit vs energetic adhesion cost). Establishes that exchange CAN select for contact given benefit>cost and partner availability; does NOT model spatial exchange PDE or membrane mechanics (M2+). The selection is regime-dependent \u2014 a frequency threshold exists (full phase map = M4).", "_lifecycle_floor": "provisional-claim"}], "runs": [{"run_id": "viva_genesis.composites.proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid.proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid__1793504556__f930ce", "spec_id": "study-selection-for-proximity", "label": "viva_genesis.composites.proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid.proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid__1793504556__f930ce", "sim_name": "viva_genesis.composites.proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid.proto_endosymbiosis_hybrid__1793504556__f930ce", "variant": null, "composite": null, "p